# Sync local with origin before edits

**Before changing any tracked file**, confirm this machine matches the remote tip. Dual-machine (Mac + Windows) both push **`test`**. Editing on a stale local is how conflicts happen.

Question-only turns do not need this check.

## Required check (every implementation turn)

```bash
git fetch origin
git status -sb
git rev-list --left-right --count HEAD...@{upstream}
```

On **`test`**, `@{upstream}` is **`origin/test`**. Use that branch’s upstream if Ryan is elsewhere.

| Result (`local` `remote`) | Do |
| --- | --- |
| `0  0` | In sync. Edit. |
| `0  N` | Behind. `git pull` (rebase if already the habit), then edit. |
| `N  0` | Ahead only. Fine if those commits are ours this session. Do not assume Windows/Mac has the same tip. |
| `N  M` | **Diverged.** Stop. Do not edit. Tell Ryan. Resolve (usually pull --rebase) before any new diff. |

## Do not

- Start implementing because “we pulled at session start.” Fetch again if anything may have landed since.
- Pull over dirty tracked files. Stop and tell Ryan if the tree is dirty **and** origin is ahead.
- Force-push to “win” a divergence.

`AGENT_RULE_SYNC_ORIGIN_BEFORE_EDIT` — searchability token.
